WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 line:92%
-Let's talk about North Korea,

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you have
this military background.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:06.740
When you hear the president
use terms like "fire and fury,"

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel as though
that's what he thinks

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone with a strong
military will would say.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
But as someone
who was in the military,

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that the kind of language
that military people use?

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. The toughest
fighters out there,

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
the operators out there,
are the quietest,

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
most understated people
you will ever meet,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, frankly,
he's not helping us

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:30.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
by engaging in this battle
of -- of terminology.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:34.100
I mean, you can't out-hyperbole
a dictator who's crazy --

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.937
a man who executed his own uncle
with an aircraft --

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
an antiaircraft machine gun.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.609 size:81% position:41%
-So Trump is not gonna
out-crazy Kim Jong-un.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:43.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stop it.
You're the Commander-in-Chief

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.945
of the greatest military
on the face of the Earth.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
Act like it.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.950 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.753 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Do you think...

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:57.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, he feels that
presenting toughness

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.825 line:92%
is the same as toughness.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that --
Do you think it's a mistake

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
to present toughness
the way he is?

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or is that --
Or is there an argument

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
that that's the smart thing
to do.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.967
When you do have
the best military in the world,

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.868 size:84% position:42% line:92%
do you let people know?

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you have to understand
that Kim Jong-un

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.640 line:92%
is trying to consolidate power.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the ways
he's doing that

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.177 size:88% position:44%
is by executing anybody
that doesn't please him.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:20.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
The other is to tell
the North Korean people,

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"You're starving,

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's because
the world wants to attack us,

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I have
to take the money that,

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
instead of giving you rice,
I'm gonna use it

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.088 line:92%
to build a nuclear weapon.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when you've got
the leader of the free world,

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
the president
of the United States,

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:33.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
engaging in this,
all you're doing is --

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.229
You're just writing
the propaganda for Kim Jong-un.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.098
All of those tweets
that Trump has been putting out,

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
or these statements,
Kim Jong-un is gonna put out

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
through his own
propaganda machine.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
He might as well
be working for him.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.604 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That doesn't help us.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think, though,
now Trump thinks --

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.176 line:92%
He probably sees these like,

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Now my tweets
are even in North Korea.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.847 size:78% position:39%
This is huge for me."
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:55.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, again,
you remember,

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're never gonna beat a guy
who fires people

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
by killing them
with antiaircraft weapons.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, now,
I also want to ask about this.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
you obviously believe --

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.192 line:92%
You have a background that leads

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
to a diverse
part of the military.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems to me
that diversity in the military

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.299 size:81% position:41% line:92%
is an important thing.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
Donald Trump said
he was doing a favor

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:18.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the military
by his trans ban --

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.639 size:81% position:41% line:92%
through his trans ban.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.406 line:92%
What do you think of that?

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you think
the president said

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the people in the military
with that choice?

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:27.380 line:92%
-He basically said that, one,

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Even if you
have served honorably,

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.617 line:92%
we don't want you anymore."

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that means that
if you are trans,

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
then you're
gonna have two choices --

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
either quit and take
your experience with you

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:38.958 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or hide who you are

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make yourself susceptible
to blackmail.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause that's what happened
under "Don't ask, don't tell."

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
Under "Don't ask, don't tell,"
a lot of folks

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
were actually
being held hostage by people

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.235 line:92%
who knew that they were gay

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
and threatened them
and threatened their careers.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.072 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So, that's not helpful.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
And on the other hand,
we have had

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:58.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
tens of thousands
of trans servicemen and women

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have served honorably,
who've bled,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.680 line:92%
who've died for this country.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.017
And to turn away people who are
willing to sacrifice for us

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.218 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is foolish at best.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I agree with that.
[ Applause ]

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:11.057 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You obviously --

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:11.724 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You served your country,

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:14.060
you sacrificed for your country
via the military.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you always make it clear,
it strikes me,

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:19.866
that there are other ways
to serve for young people.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:23.436
You don't necessarily
have to do it via the military.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give us some other ideas
of how you think

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.539 line:92%
people can serve this country?

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well,
I've introduced legislation,

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:30.343 size:88% position:44%
along with Seth Moulton
and the great John Lewis

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.745 size:84% position:42%
that would allow people
to earn, for example,

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:33.980 line:92%
college money for service.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
You should be able to pick up
chalk, a hammer,

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.786
a ladle at a soup kitchen
and earn college money

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
just as much
as I picked up a rifle

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.423 line:92%
and earned college money.

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.290 line:92%
We all have a chance to serve.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even if just once a year
you go out volunteer,

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.327 size:84% position:42% line:92%
you're doing something.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:50.430
Less than one-half of 1% of this
nation wears the uniform,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:54.033
and that's an awful big load
for a small percentage to carry.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
So let's all do
a little carrying.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
Doesn't mean you have
to go join the military.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.371 size:75% position:38%
Doesn't mean you got
to go get blown up.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:00.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
God forbid.
I tried not to get blown up.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:03.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
But --
Didn't work too well, but...

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.012 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But do something.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.113 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Do something.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.348 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:09.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How much longer
a break do you have?

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
When do you have
to go back to D.C.?

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.385 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I'm going back tonight.

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're going back
to D.C. tonight?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought you guys
had a recess now. No?

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:16.956 line:92%
-Well, people call it a recess,

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:19.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's actually
a district work period.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:19.993 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'm traveling the state.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:22.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was out in --
on a river barge

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:24.664 line:92%
on the Mississippi 48 hours ago,

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.332
and now I'm here, and I'm
going back home tomorrow.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.969
-"Recess" sounds so much better
than "district work period."

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:30.536 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:31.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought
I was getting a recess,

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.673 size:84% position:42%
but then they told me,
"Here's your schedule."

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Wait.
That's not right."

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:36.809 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-"That's not recess!

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought
we were playing dodgeball."

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:43.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
Continued luck in Washington.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
Senator Tammy Duckworth,
everybody!

